[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2952598322","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107242#issuecomment-2952598322","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107242","id":2952598322,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6v_RMy","user":{"login":"RedMser","id":5117197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTcxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5117197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser","html_url":"https://github.com/RedMser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-07T14:51:15Z","updated_at":"2025-06-07T14:51:15Z","body":"Looks great!\r\n\r\nIMO I think it would be easier to get this feature merged if the new resizable scroll bar was not yet exposed to scripting. I see some parts aren't implemented yet, and the class' APIs would likely need a new proposal as well. \r\nIf the classes are exposed, breaking changes to the API become harder.\r\nBut if it's just used internally by the editor for now, the feature to zoom animation player can be implemented without worrying about the scripting side of things yet.\r\n\r\nOnce user demand is there for this class in scripting, it can be reconsidered.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2952598322/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2952940946","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107242#issuecomment-2952940946","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107242","id":2952940946,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wAk2S","user":{"login":"Chenyang341","id":88185353,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTg1MzUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88185353?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341","html_url":"https://github.com/Chenyang341","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-07T19:55:55Z","updated_at":"2025-06-07T19:55:55Z","body":"Thanks for the feedback! Yes I think that it is a good idea to not expose it to scripting yet. Would it be enough to remove the added lines in register_scene_types.cpp and the .xml files?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2952940946/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2952971104","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107242#issuecomment-2952971104","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107242","id":2952971104,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wAsNg","user":{"login":"RedMser","id":5117197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTcxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5117197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser","html_url":"https://github.com/RedMser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-07T20:25:35Z","updated_at":"2025-06-07T20:25:35Z","body":"> Would it be enough to remove the added lines in register_scene_types.cpp and the .xml files?\r\n\r\nYeah I think so.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2952971104/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2953566355","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107242#issuecomment-2953566355","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107242","id":2953566355,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wC9iT","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-08T05:19:00Z","updated_at":"2025-06-08T05:19:00Z","body":"I'm so happy to see progress on this! 😄 \r\n\r\nHowever, I do see that at about 0:05 in your video, you begin dragging the left handle inwards, but the right bound in the main view zooms in as well. IMO, the right bound should stay fixed where it is, like so:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f1462454-98e4-4731-b845-b15275a13216\r\n\r\n(Note that in this video, the right bound stays constant at about frame 310.) Currently I can only confirm that's how it works in Blender, but from what I remember, all other software I've used with these kinds of scroll bars do the same thing.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2953566355/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2954075822","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107242#issuecomment-2954075822","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107242","id":2954075822,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wE56u","user":{"login":"Chenyang341","id":88185353,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTg1MzUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88185353?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341","html_url":"https://github.com/Chenyang341","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-08T13:20:05Z","updated_at":"2025-06-08T13:20:05Z","body":"I was uncertain about this too. In godot the extra time visible after the max time (in this case 20 seconds) is dependent in the zoom value, so when I pull the left handle inwards the extra time decreases, therefore necessary to adjust the right bound. But if the right bound is lower than the max time it stays in the same place, it is shown in the video at around 0:16.\r\n\r\nI didn't know if it was a good idea to change the way the max visible time was calculated so I left it as it was.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2954075822/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2999562515","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107242#issuecomment-2999562515","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107242","id":2999562515,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yybET","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-24T09:36:23Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T09:36:23Z","body":"The new class should be in `editor/gui`, because it's only used in editor. Likewise, the theme definitions should be moved to editor theme.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2999562515/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2999600963","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107242#issuecomment-2999600963","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107242","id":2999600963,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yykdD","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-24T09:48:53Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T09:48:53Z","body":"I tested the feature and it seems to work fine for the most part. As other already mentioned, it would be better if moving one side of the scrollbar did not move the other. The worst part of the current behavior is that the other side always moves to the right, so when you drag right side of the scrollbar it shrinks additionally, and expands when dragging left side.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eb48382b-4dcc-4446-8d03-ede227bb0364\r\n\r\nAlso not sure what to do about the old zoom slider. It feels redundant, but the new scrollbar does not cover all zoom levels, so it's not like we can just remove it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2999600963/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3001739477","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107242#issuecomment-3001739477","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107242","id":3001739477,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6y6ujV","user":{"login":"Chenyang341","id":88185353,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTg1MzUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88185353?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341","html_url":"https://github.com/Chenyang341","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-24T20:14:20Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T20:14:20Z","body":"Thanks! I will be changing according to the feedbacks.\r\n\r\nAs for the moving of one side of the scrollbar when moving the other side, it is because when changing the zoom, the extra time visible in the timeline after the max time also changes. When pulling one handle, the other stays in the same value of time in the timeline, but it needs to compensate due to the change of the extra visible time, therefore moving it. This could be resolved if the extra time visible was a fixed value (for example 10% of the max time, so if the max time was 20s, it would have 2s of extra visible time, extending the timeline to 22s), then the scrollbar wouldn't need to compensate for the change of the extra time. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3001739477/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3006461410","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107242#issuecomment-3006461410","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107242","id":3006461410,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6zMvXi","user":{"login":"Chenyang341","id":88185353,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTg1MzUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88185353?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341","html_url":"https://github.com/Chenyang341","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chenyang341/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-25T22:50:53Z","updated_at":"2025-06-25T22:50:53Z","body":"I have changed it so the extra time at the end stays the same, 20% of the total time (adding 4 seconds in this case). This way one side of the scrollbar no longer moves when the other side is being pulled. \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e6252cc3-0dca-444c-83eb-7510ca4a2188\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3006461410/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3544606041","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107242#issuecomment-3544606041","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107242","id":3544606041,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TRmVZ","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-18T01:11:47Z","updated_at":"2025-11-18T01:11:47Z","body":"Hi, I know it's been a while since the last update on this but since we're now in the feature phase of 4.6, I was wondering what the status of this PR was? The last video looks good to me!\r\n\r\nIf you're unable to or don't want to continue working on the PR, I'd be happy to try taking it over as well 🙂 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3544606041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github